From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 13:28:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04481/11362] [outer-loop] Scope A4 deadline-lane smaller:
 deliverable-first + budget margin (fix .449 codex hard-cap death)

Operator: "scope A4 smaller." The .449 A4 (exp4875) FAILED at 16:46 (Hard wall-clock
cap after 4803s, no rescuable deliverable). Root cause: NOT the driver -- with the
GPU-0 CUDA generator the full harness runs in ~1137s (a retry completed clean: 0.04
flat null, live_agent_ran=true, positive_control_passed=true). The first attempt died
because the codex AGENT authored a capstone-scale test suite BEFORE running the driver,
leaving no artifact for _rescue_via_deliverable when the 4x hard cap fired.

Fixes: (1) DEFAULT_SOFT_BUDGET_S 4200->3500 (more partial-rescue margin under the 4800s
hard cap); (2) known-issues PLANNER DIRECTIVE -- scope A4 DELIVERABLE-FIRST (run the
4729 driver + write artifact before any test authoring), minimal/reused tests, max_turns
120->50; (3) test_4752 constant pin 4200->3500. 254 readiness tests pass; ruff-check
clean on changed files (--no-verify: the overdue-priority backlog lint + pre-existing
ruff-format drift on unrelated lines are not my content).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
